Certainly! Here's a simple 1-bit adder in Verilog:
```verilog
module adder_1bit (input a, input b, input cin, output sum, output cout);
  assign sum = a ^ b ^ cin;
  assign cout = (a & b) | (b & cin) | (a & cin);
endmodule
```
This module takes two 1-bit inputs `a` and `b`, and a carry-in `cin`, and produces a sum and a carry-out. The `^` operator is used for XOR, and the `&` operator is used for AND. The carry-out is generated if any two of the three inputs are 1.
